"footer.rights":"All rights reserved","footer.contactMore":"Contact Us to Ask More Information About Your Project","co.hero.title":"70 years plus of workspaces manufacturing","co.hero.body":"The story of Codutti began in the 1950s, when three brothers joined forces in a modest village workshop. Since then, Codutti has built a legacy of quality and prestige, becoming a benchmark brand in the luxury office furniture market — specialising in Essential, Operative and Executive collections designed and manufactured entirely in-house.","co.who.title":"Who We Are","co.who.body1":"Attention to detail and product reliability led the company to provide the furnishings for two icons of the Italian fleet in the 1960s: the Raffaello and Michelangelo cruise ships. Over the years, Codutti has refined its passion for producing high-end furniture, specialising particularly in the office sector — introducing meticulous craftsmanship in leather and hides alongside its traditional wooden offerings.","co.who.body2":"Today Codutti designs, engineers and manufactures every collection at its own production facilities in Friuli Venezia Giulia, combining CNC precision on wood and metal components with hand-finished leather detailing — a method that lets us customise nearly every element of a project without compromising on consistency or lead time.","co.history.title":"History & Brand Evolution","co.history.1954":"Three brothers found the original workshop in Friuli Venezia Giulia, laying the foundations of what would become Codutti.","co.history.1960s":"Codutti furnishes the Raffaello and Michelangelo — two icons of the Italian cruise fleet — establishing the brand as a benchmark for quality and prestige.","co.history.8090s":"The company deepens its specialisation in the office sector, expanding in-house production of executive and operative furniture.","co.history.2000s":"Introduction of contract and bespoke project capabilities, supporting architecture firms and general contractors on large-scale turnkey fit-outs worldwide.","co.history.2020s":"Launch of the Essential, Operative and Executive collection architecture, and continued investment in acoustic solutions and adjustable systems for the modern office.","co.history.2026":"Codutti continues to exhibit internationally — from Fuori Salone in Milan to Clerkenwell Design Week in London — while publishing the Codutti Journal on design, craftsmanship and workspace culture.","co.vmv.title":"Vision, Mission & Values","co.vmv.visionTitle":"Contemporary Vision","co.vmv.visionBody":"To be the international benchmark for Made-in-Italy luxury executive furniture — where seventy years of craftsmanship meet the precision of new technology.","co.vmv.missionTitle":"Crafted Mission","co.vmv.missionBody":"To transform every office into a high-end space, uniting functionality and impeccable aesthetics in furniture built to last.","co.vmv.valuesTitle":"Contract Values","co.vmv.valuesBody":"Uncompromising quality, attention to detail, respect for materials and people, and a deep sense of Italian roots guide every decision we make.","co.projects.title":"Projects We've Taken Part In","co.projects.body":"From furnishing the Raffaello and Michelangelo cruise ships in the 1960s to today's contract and bespoke fit-outs for architecture firms and companies worldwide, Codutti has taken part in projects across offices, boardrooms and shared spaces of every scale.","co.projects.discoverAll":"Discover All the Projects","co.certs.title":"Certifications","co.certs.body":"Our production is certified to the standards our contract and international clients require, covering quality management and responsible sourcing of raw materials.","co.certs.iso":"Quality management system certification covering design and manufacturing.","co.certs.fscTitle":"FSC® Chain of Custody","co.certs.fsc":"Responsibly sourced timber, tracked from forest to finished piece.","co.certs.mii":"Every collection is designed and manufactured entirely at our facilities in Friuli Venezia Giulia.","co.certs.consultAll":"Consult All Our Certifications","co.locations.title":"Our Locations","allProducts.title":"Our Products, Spaces and Solutions","allProducts.intro":"Three ways to furnish a space, from fast-moving everyday offices to flagship boardrooms — browse by line, or use the categories above to go straight to a product type.","allProducts.discoverSolutions":"Discover the Solutions","contact.hero.title":"Contact Us","contact.hero.body":"Reach our general contacts below, send a specific request, or get in touch directly with the right person on our team.","contact.locations.title":"Our Locations","news.hero.title":"News and Events","news.hero.body":"Everything happening at Codutti in one place — new collections and finishes as they launch, the trade fairs and design weeks where you can see them in person, and the ongoing story of a company that's been building office furniture entirely in-house in Friuli Venezia Giulia since 1954. Browse the latest below, or search the full archive for a specific story.","news.latestUpdates.title":"Latest Updates","news.events.title":"Events"
